@startuml
title F10 - Away, pause and visitor modes
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #2877B5
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #17324D
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #F4F7FA
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFF1BF
skinparam NoteBorderColor #9C6500
autonumber
actor "Primary caregiver" as Caregiver
boundary "A03\nApp routines" as A03
control "B02\nHome/consent" as B02
control "H07\nHub lifecycle/config" as H07
control "H06\nHub resident interface" as H06
control "H05\nHub rules adapter" as H05
control "S02\nDeterministic rules core" as S02
boundary "A02\nApp home" as A02
Caregiver -> A03: Select HOME, AWAY, PAUSED or VISITOR with reason/expiry
A03 -> B02: Submit authorized versioned mode command
B02 -> H07: Publish desired configuration
H07 -> H07: Atomically apply newer valid version
H07 -> H06: Update local mode/privacy feedback
H07 -> H05: Update active routine mode
H05 -> S02: Gate incident evaluation by mode
S02 --> H05: Return suppression reason outside HOME
B02 -> A02: Expose current/applied mode and freshness
note over Caregiver,A02: Expiry or stale desired state must not silently reactivate monitoring.
note over Caregiver,A02: Outcome - Mode changes are explicit, versioned and visible; routines never generate missing-activity incidents in an ineligible mode.
@enduml
